  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Hana set her wiping cloth down on the side table and straightened, a ready smile softening the request. \"Thank you, Ted. Just inside the door, beside the shoe rack, would be perfect. That way it isn't underfoot, and you can find it easily whenever you need it.\" She gestured toward the small open space left of the entrance. \"No rush at all—come in whenever you're ready.\"\n\nMia paused with a stack of small plates balanced against her chest, her weight shifting back as she cast a quick look down the hallway. \"The left side near the kitchen counter is the route I'm using—if that stays open, I can bring the rest out without backing into anything.\" She offered a small, careful smile. \"Thank you for checking.\"",
